- **Category**: perf
- **Planned at**: commit `56d794a2`, 2026-10-19

## Why this matters

The whole parsed import preview — every row, every field diff, plus a per-row `wire:model` binding — lives in a **public Livewire property** and is rendered in full. The accepted upload size is 10 MB, so a large sheet can be tens of thousands of rows: every Livewire round trip while the preview is open (toggling one row, opening help, confirming) serializes the entire array, ships it, and re-renders the entire DOM. Bounding the preview to a paged window and keeping the row decisions server-side makes the page usable for large
